  "title": "ReCBM and Concept Integrity in CBMs",
  "summary": "ReCBM introduces uncertainty-gated relational reasoning to enhance concept bottleneck models (CBMs) by addressing the lack of robust reasoning under unreliable concept states. It introduces semantically defined concept relations and uses uncertainty to guide refinement, improving both concept and task recovery without degrading downstream performance. Concept integrity is proposed as a complementary criterion for evaluating CBMs.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "ReCBM improves concept and task recovery under missing and flipped concepts, supported uncertainty-aware intervention, and extracts compact task-relevant concept subsets.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Concept integrity is proposed as a complementary representation-level criterion, with the concept integrity score (CIS) differing from task and concept accuracy rankings.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The latent decoupled concept bottleneck model (LDCBM) retains approximately 93% of full-label task performance with only 10% of concept labels.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
